NAME: lifecycle
LAST DEPLOYED: Sun Sep 20 00:47:58 2026
NAMESPACE: lifecycle
STATUS: deployed
REVISION: 1
DESCRIPTION: Install complete
TEST SUITE: None
NOTES:
edgelab-hub 0.1.0 deployed as lifecycle-edgelab-hub

1. Populate the origin PVC with signed releases (from a machine that has the
   publisher key), e.g.:

   kubectl exec deploy/lifecycle-edgelab-hub -it -- sh -c "edgelab publish --help"
   # or copy objects: kubectl cp work/origin/. deploy/lifecycle-edgelab-hub:/origin/

   The origin is mounted READ-ONLY in the hub pod; publish from elsewhere or
   via a separate publisher pod that owns the same PVC read-write.

2. Notifier credentials come from the secret "edgelab-notifiers"
   (keys: telegram-token, telegram-chat, slack-webhook). Create it only when
   you have real credentials; without it the hub runs with notifications off:

   kubectl create secret generic edgelab-notifiers \
     --from-literal=telegram-token=... --from-literal=telegram-chat=... \
     --from-literal=slack-webhook=...

3. Admin plane: unix socket at /state/admin.sock (under /state):

   kubectl exec deploy/lifecycle-edgelab-hub -- \
     edgelab-tui --admin /state/admin.sock --json

4. Health: kubectl get pods -l app.kubernetes.io/name=edgelab-hub
